  "body": "Part of #361. Vendor tool STEP packages commonly carry named coordinate systems that place the cutting point and the mounting interface (the ISO 13399 / GTC convention). Read them when present, so a vendor body is aligned automatically instead of by hand-entered offsets. When they are absent or ambiguous, fall back to the numeric placement with a note that names why.\n\nSources are limited to published vendor and standard material. The coordinate-system names must be confirmed from public GTC documentation before any code; no guessing.\n\n**Done means:** a test STEP with tool coordinate systems aligns with no manual offsets; one without them falls back by name.\n",
